{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_03f8569485436378016a958342003c87d2a50ab66269d163bc\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"b1c86e0d-4c01-4bd9-90ba-51112244a75e\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"b1c86e0d-4c01-4bd9-90ba-51112244a75e\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_AVNolbjqXf9HU0vb8Pz89b4M|fc_03f8569485436378016a958396cc8087d28e60779df007b8b6","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing module map","path":"out/module_map.json","content":"{\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/cli.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Packaging entry point that loads environment settings, initializes the SQLite schema, and prints readiness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.config\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/config.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Defines Settings and maps environment variables into runtime configuration values.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.models\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/models.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Defines the Order dataclass shared between handlers, audit logic, and persistence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/audit.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Builds in-memory audit event payloads for order create and read responses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/storage/repo.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Implements SQLite-backed order schema creation, inserts, and lookups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Implements order create and read use-cases over repository and audit helpers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Registers HTTP route callbacks that adapt app requests to handler functions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entry_points\": [\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"kind\": \"cli\",\n      \"exposure\": \"Declared in pyproject.toml [project.scripts] as the minisvc console entry point.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n      \"kind\": \"http_registration\",\n      \"exposure\": \"Import-and-call integration hook for wiring POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id> onto an external app object.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"kind\": \"http_handler\",\n      \"exposure\": \"POST /orders handler target via minisvc.api.routes:register_routes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n      \"kind\": \"http_handler\",\n      \"exposure\": \"GET /orders/<order_id> handler target via minisvc.api.routes:register_routes.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dependency_edges\": [\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.config\",\n      \"type\": \"imports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n      \"type\": \"calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"to\": \"os.environ\",\n      \"type\": \"reads_config\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\",\n      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n      \"type\": \"calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n      \"type\": \"imports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"type\": \"calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n      \"type\": \"calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n      \"type\": \"imports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n      \"type\": \"imports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n      \"type\": \"imports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\",\n      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n      \"type\": \"calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n      \"type\": \"calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n      \"type\": \"calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n      \"type\": \"imports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\",\n      \"to\": \"sqlite3\",\n      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n      \"to\": \"MINISVC_DB\",\n      \"type\": \"reads_config\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n      \"to\": \"MINISVC_READONLY\",\n      \"type\": \"reads_config\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"key_functions\": [\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"kind\": \"function\",\n      \"summary\": \"Loads Settings from environment, constructs OrderRepository, initializes schema, and emits a readiness message.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"argv=None\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"int status code 0\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"No command-line arguments are consumed.\", \"Read-only configuration is loaded but not enforced here.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n      \"kind\": \"function\",\n      \"summary\": \"Builds a Settings dataclass from environment variables with defaults.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"env: dict[str, str]\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"Settings(database_path, readonly)\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Defaults database_path to orders.sqlite.\", \"Treats MINISVC_READONLY=1 as true.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n      \"kind\": \"method\",\n      \"summary\": \"Creates the single orders table if it does not already exist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [],\n      \"outputs\": [\"None\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Schema contains only order_id, customer, and total_cents.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n      \"kind\": \"method\",\n      \"summary\": \"Inserts one Order row into SQLite without retry or conflict handling.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"order: Order\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"None\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Duplicate primary keys or SQLite write errors propagate.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n      \"kind\": \"method\",\n      \"summary\": \"Loads one order row by id and materializes it into an Order dataclass.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"order_id: str\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"Order | None\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Returns None when no row exists.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"kind\": \"function\",\n      \"summary\": \"Transforms payload fields into an Order, persists it, and returns a created response with an inline audit event.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"payload: dict\", \"repo: OrderRepository\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"dict response\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Assumes payload contains order_id, customer, and total_cents.\", \"Casts total_cents with int() and does not catch validation or persistence failures.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n      \"kind\": \"function\",\n      \"summary\": \"Fetches an order, returns missing when absent, otherwise returns order data plus a read audit event.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"order_id: str\", \"repo: OrderRepository\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"dict response\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Read path emits an event in the response but does not persist audit state.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n      \"kind\": \"function\",\n      \"summary\": \"Wires handler lambdas onto an app object exposing post() and get() methods.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"app\", \"repo\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"None\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Route registration assumes an external framework supplies the app abstraction.\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n      \"kind\": \"function\",\n      \"summary\": \"Builds the audit event dictionary returned from handlers.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"order: Order\", \"action: str\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"dict event\"],\n      \"notes\": [\"Pure function; no durable side effects.\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"runtime_flows\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CLI startup flow\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"Packaging invokes minisvc.cli:main via the minisvc console script declared in pyproject.toml.\",\n        \"main reads os.environ and passes it to minisvc.config:load_settings.\",\n        \"load_settings returns Settings(database_path, readonly).\",\n        \"main instantiates minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository with settings.database_path.\",\n        \"main calls OrderRepository.init_schema to create the orders table if missing.\",\n        \"main prints a readiness line containing the database path and returns status code 0.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HTTP create-order flow\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"An integrator calls minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo).\",\n        \"register_routes wires POST /orders to minisvc.api.handlers:create_order via a lambda that forwards payload and repo.\",\n        \"create_order reads order_id, customer, and total_cents from the request payload.\",\n        \"create_order instantiates minisvc.models:Order after coercing total_cents with int().\",\n        \"create_order calls OrderRepository.save, which opens a sqlite3 connection and inserts the row into orders.\",\n        \"create_order calls minisvc.audit:order_event with action='created'.\",\n        \"create_order returns a response dict containing status, order_id, and the inline event payload.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HTTP get-order flow\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"register_routes wires GET /orders/<order_id> to minisvc.api.handlers:get_order.\",\n        \"get_order calls OrderRepository.get(order_id).\",\n        \"OrderRepository.get queries SQLite for a matching row and returns Order or None.\",\n        \"get_order returns status='missing' when the row is absent.\",\n        \"When the row exists, get_order serializes order.__dict__, adds order_event(action='read'), and returns status='ok'.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"},"intent":"Writing module map"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_oIKyuH6kOjZvW2RKLbZANghT|fc_03f8569485436378016a958396cc9487d297e4685cd68c3f72","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing architecture summary","path":"out/architecture.md","content":"# minisvc architecture\n\n## What is active runtime code\n- `minisvc/cli.py`: real startup path. `minisvc.cli:main` is the console-script entry point declared in `pyproject.toml`.\n- `minisvc/config.py`: real configuration loader for `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`: real persistence layer. Owns schema creation plus order insert/read queries.\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`: real use-case logic for create/read order flows.\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py`: real integration hook that registers HTTP routes onto an external app object.\n- `minisvc/audit.py`: real helper that builds response-local audit event payloads.\n- `minisvc/models.py`: real shared data model.\n\n## What is not business logic\n- `minisvc/__init__.py`, `minisvc/api/__init__.py`, `minisvc/storage/__init__.py`: package markers only. No runtime behavior.\n- `pyproject.toml`: packaging metadata plus console-script declaration.\n- `README.md`: documentation only; some claims do not match code.\n\n## Module map\n| Module | Purpose | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `minisvc.cli` | Bootstrap the service runtime. | Loads settings, creates repository, initializes SQLite schema, prints readiness. |\n| `minisvc.config` | Convert environment variables into `Settings`. | Supports `MINISVC_DB`; parses `MINISVC_READONLY=1` to `readonly=True`. |\n| `minisvc.models` | Define `Order`. | `dataclass` used across API and storage layers. |\n| `minisvc.storage.repo` | Persist and fetch orders in SQLite. | One table: `orders(order_id, customer, total_cents)`. |\n| `minisvc.api.handlers` | Implement create/read order use-cases. | No HTTP framework dependency beyond input/output dicts. |\n| `minisvc.api.routes` | Adapt handlers to an app/router object. | Expects `app.post()` and `app.get()` methods. |\n| `minisvc.audit` | Build audit event dicts. | Pure helper; no storage side effects. |\n\n## Entry points\n- `minisvc.cli:main`: executable console entry point.\n- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`: API integration entry point for wiring routes.\n- Routed handler targets:\n  - `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`\n  - `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`\n\n## Data flow\n### CLI startup\n1. `minisvc.cli:main` reads `os.environ`.\n2. `minisvc.config:load_settings` builds `Settings(database_path, readonly)`.\n3. `main` constructs `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n4. `OrderRepository.init_schema()` creates the `orders` table if needed.\n5. `main` prints `minisvc ready at ...` and exits `0`.\n\n### HTTP create-order flow\n1. Integrator calls `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo)`.\n2. `register_routes` binds `POST /orders` to `create_order(payload, repo)`.\n3. `create_order` pulls `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` from the payload.\n4. It creates `Order(...)`, coercing `total_cents` with `int()`.\n5. It calls `OrderRepository.save(order)`.\n6. `save` opens SQLite and inserts the row.\n7. `create_order` returns `{status, order_id, event}` where `event` comes from `minisvc.audit:order_event`.\n\n### HTTP read flow\n1. `register_routes` binds `GET /orders/<order_id>` to `get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n2. `get_order` calls `repo.get(order_id)`.\n3. Missing row -> `{status: \"missing\", order_id}`.\n4. Present row -> `{status: \"ok\", order: order.__dict__, event: order_event(..., \"read\")}`.\n\n## Storage\n- Backend: SQLite via the standard-library `sqlite3` module.\n- File location: `Settings.database_path`, default `orders.sqlite` in the current working directory.\n- Schema: exactly one durable table, `orders`.\n- No repository abstraction beyond `OrderRepository`; each method opens a fresh connection.\n- No audit table. Audit data exists only in returned response dicts.\n\n## Risks and extension points\n### Risks\n- Read-only mode is parsed but never enforced. Any caller with a repository can still write through `create_order`.\n- `create_order` has no validation guardrails beyond `int(total_cents)`. Missing keys, non-integer totals, duplicate IDs, and SQLite write failures propagate as exceptions.\n- No retry behavior around `repo.save()`. Transient SQLite failures fail the request immediately.\n- Audit events are not durable. Process restarts lose all audit history because only the `orders` table exists.\n- Route wiring depends on an external app shape but provides no adapter contract or framework-specific integration tests.\n\n### Extension points\n- Add validation and error translation in `minisvc.api.handlers` before persistence.\n- Enforce `Settings.readonly` either in handlers or repository methods.\n- Add durable audit persistence beside `OrderRepository` or inside a widened repository transaction.\n- Replace the lambda wrappers in `minisvc.api.routes` with framework-native handlers once an actual web stack is chosen.\n"},"intent":"Writing architecture summary"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1344,"output":4716,"cacheRead":22016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28076,"reasoningTokens":536,"cost":{"input":0.00336,"output":0.07074,"cacheRead":0.005503999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.079604}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788183360747,"responseId":"resp_03f8569485436378016a9583412d7487d29bd60b550b88b6d4","duration":86756.29956799999,"ttft":1295.061296999993},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_AVNolbjqXf9HU0vb8Pz89b4M|fc_03f8569485436378016a958396cc8087d28e60779df007b8b6","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/module_map.json#F78D]\nSuccessfully wrote 9788 bytes to out/module_map.json"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/module_map.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788183447520},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_oIKyuH6kOjZvW2RKLbZANghT|fc_03f8569485436378016a958396cc9487d297e4685cd68c3f72","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/architecture.md#42F5]\nSuccessfully wrote 4715 bytes to out/architecture.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/architecture.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788183447541}]}
