{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"{\"i\":\"Writing risk register\",\"path\":\"out/risk_register.csv\",\"content\":\"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\\nR1,storage/data durability,\\\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:init_schema creates only orders; save/get open a new sqlite3 connection per call against a local file path\\\",\\\"Durability depends on a single local SQLite file with no backup, no journaling policy configuration, and no transaction spanning related writes.\\\",\\\"Define operational backup/restore expectations, set explicit SQLite pragmas if needed, and add integration coverage for crash/restart expectations.\\\",backend-platform\\nR2,audit behavior,\\\"minisvc/audit.py:order_event is a pure dict builder and minisvc/storage/repo.py has no audit table or audit write path\\\",\\\"No durable audit history exists after process exit, so security/compliance review and post-incident reconstruction are weak.\\\",\\\"Persist audit records in SQLite or another store and verify create/read flows write them atomically with business events where required.\\\",backend-owner\\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\\\"minisvc/config.py:load_settings defaults MINISVC_DB to orders.sqlite and minisvc/cli.py:main uses current process environment and working directory\\\",\\\"Deployments can silently write to an unexpected relative path, and readonly configuration creates false confidence because the flag is not enforced.\\\",\\\"Require explicit database paths in deployment config, document cwd expectations, and either enforce or remove the readonly setting.\\\",ops-backend\\nR4,API input validation,\\\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int() without catching exceptions\\\",\\\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError, producing framework-level 500s instead of controlled client errors.\\\",\\\"Add request validation, type checks, and exception-to-response mapping at the handler or adapter boundary.\\\",api-owner\\nR5,persistence error handling,\\\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:save performs one insert and minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order has no retry or sqlite error translation\\\",\\\"Duplicate order IDs and transient SQLite errors propagate as raw exceptions and may break API contracts.\\\",\\\"Translate sqlite exceptions into stable application errors and add targeted retries only where idempotency is clear.\\\",backend-owner\\nR6,integration contract,\\\"minisvc/api/routes.py:register_routes assumes app.post() and app.get() plus payload/order_id callback signatures but defines no interface or tests\\\",\\\"A framework integration can mismatch callback signatures or path parameter behavior without early detection.\\\",\\\"Document the adapter contract and add a thin integration test with the chosen web framework.\\\",api-owner\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bBgBXCBILMuV1e0gImR8CjKc|fc_03f8569485436378016a9583bbe03487d2a491171863f46d69","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing risk register","path":"out/risk_register.csv","content":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:init_schema creates only orders; save/get open a new sqlite3 connection per call against a local file path\",\"Durability depends on a single local SQLite file with no backup, no journaling policy configuration, and no transaction spanning related writes.\",\"Define operational backup/restore expectations, set explicit SQLite pragmas if needed, and add integration coverage for crash/restart expectations.\",backend-platform\nR2,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:order_event is a pure dict builder and minisvc/storage/repo.py has no audit table or audit write path\",\"No durable audit history exists after process exit, so security/compliance review and post-incident reconstruction are weak.\",\"Persist audit records in SQLite or another store and verify create/read flows write them atomically with business events where required.\",backend-owner\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:load_settings defaults MINISVC_DB to orders.sqlite and minisvc/cli.py:main uses current process environment and working directory\",\"Deployments can silently write to an unexpected relative path, and readonly configuration creates false confidence because the flag is not enforced.\",\"Require explicit database paths in deployment config, document cwd expectations, and either enforce or remove the readonly setting.\",ops-backend\nR4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int() without catching exceptions\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError, producing framework-level 500s instead of controlled client errors.\",\"Add request validation, type checks, and exception-to-response mapping at the handler or adapter boundary.\",api-owner\nR5,persistence error handling,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:save performs one insert and minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order has no retry or sqlite error translation\",\"Duplicate order IDs and transient SQLite errors propagate as raw exceptions and may break API contracts.\",\"Translate sqlite exceptions into stable application errors and add targeted retries only where idempotency is clear.\",backend-owner\nR6,integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:register_routes assumes app.post() and app.get() plus payload/order_id callback signatures but defines no interface or tests\",\"A framework integration can mismatch callback signatures or path parameter behavior without early detection.\",\"Document the adapter contract and add a thin integration test with the chosen web framework.\",api-owner\n"}}}}
