{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_03f8569485436378016a958398964887d2a8e9aa3c6f080e06\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"b1c86e0d-4c01-4bd9-90ba-51112244a75e\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"b1c86e0d-4c01-4bd9-90ba-51112244a75e\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_G2RzIl6g0FUgQxbcZLzWgA6c|fc_03f8569485436378016a9583bbe01c87d293c4226720cd5fa0","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing discrepancy CSV","path":"out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","content":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md design note\",\"minisvc/config.py:load_settings parses readonly but minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order always calls repo.save(order); verified by exercised flow creating order 'o-ro' with Settings.readonly=True and row persisted into orders table\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may assume maintenance mode prevents writes when it does not.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md design note\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order calls repo.save(order) exactly once and minisvc/storage/repo.py:save performs one sqlite insert with no loop, retry helper, or exception handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures surface immediately and callers will not get the documented retry behavior.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md design note\",\"minisvc/audit.py:order_event only returns a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:init_schema creates only the orders table; verified SQLite schema after create flow contains [('orders',)]\",\"contradicted\",\"There is no durable audit trail for compliance, debugging, or incident review.\"\n\"This service accepts orders through a small HTTP adapter and a CLI bootstrap command\",\"README.md opening summary\",\"minisvc/cli.py:main is a real console entry point and minisvc/api/routes.py:register_routes wires POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id> onto an injected app object\",\"confirmed\",\"Low: summary matches the available entry points, though the HTTP server itself must be supplied by an integrator.\"\n\"The code in this fixture is authoritative when documentation and implementation disagree\",\"README.md note\",\"Repository code is internally consistent with observed runtime behavior from minisvc.cli:main and the create/get order flow\",\"confirmed\",\"Low: follow code over docs when triaging behavior.\"\n"},"intent":"Writing discrepancy CSV"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bBgBXCBILMuV1e0gImR8CjKc|fc_03f8569485436378016a9583bbe03487d2a491171863f46d69","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing risk register","path":"out/risk_register.csv","content":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:init_schema creates only orders; save/get open a new sqlite3 connection per call against a local file path\",\"Durability depends on a single local SQLite file with no backup, no journaling policy configuration, and no transaction spanning related writes.\",\"Define operational backup/restore expectations, set explicit SQLite pragmas if needed, and add integration coverage for crash/restart expectations.\",backend-platform\nR2,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:order_event is a pure dict builder and minisvc/storage/repo.py has no audit table or audit write path\",\"No durable audit history exists after process exit, so security/compliance review and post-incident reconstruction are weak.\",\"Persist audit records in SQLite or another store and verify create/read flows write them atomically with business events where required.\",backend-owner\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:load_settings defaults MINISVC_DB to orders.sqlite and minisvc/cli.py:main uses current process environment and working directory\",\"Deployments can silently write to an unexpected relative path, and readonly configuration creates false confidence because the flag is not enforced.\",\"Require explicit database paths in deployment config, document cwd expectations, and either enforce or remove the readonly setting.\",ops-backend\nR4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int() without catching exceptions\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError, producing framework-level 500s instead of controlled client errors.\",\"Add request validation, type checks, and exception-to-response mapping at the handler or adapter boundary.\",api-owner\nR5,persistence error handling,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:save performs one insert and minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order has no retry or sqlite error translation\",\"Duplicate order IDs and transient SQLite errors propagate as raw exceptions and may break API contracts.\",\"Translate sqlite exceptions into stable application errors and add targeted retries only where idempotency is clear.\",backend-owner\nR6,integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:register_routes assumes app.post() and app.get() plus payload/order_id callback signatures but defines no interface or tests\",\"A framework integration can mismatch callback signatures or path parameter behavior without early detection.\",\"Document the adapter contract and add a thin integration test with the chosen web framework.\",api-owner\n"},"intent":"Writing risk register"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_pk9YjAcJjjKDPuFINdSmiDod|fc_03f8569485436378016a9583bbe04487d2bf4d26af18947841","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing onboarding plan","path":"out/onboarding_plan.md","content":"# Onboarding plan\n\n## Start with the active code, not the markers\nRead these first:\n1. `README.md` for intent and known doc drift.\n2. `pyproject.toml` to see the only packaged entry point: `minisvc.cli:main`.\n3. `minisvc/cli.py` to understand startup and schema initialization.\n4. `minisvc/config.py` to see runtime knobs: `MINISVC_DB`, `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n5. `minisvc/storage/repo.py` to see the real persistence model and schema.\n6. `minisvc/api/handlers.py` to see create/read behavior, validation gaps, and persistence calls.\n7. `minisvc/api/routes.py` to see how an external HTTP adapter wires handlers.\n8. `minisvc/audit.py` and `minisvc/models.py` last; both are small supporting files.\n\nDo not spend time on these early:\n- `minisvc/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/api/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/__init__.py`\n\nThose are package markers, not business logic.\n\n## Local run commands\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```bash\npython3 -c \"from minisvc.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\"\n```\n\nThat is the most direct local startup command. `python3 -m minisvc.cli` only imports the module because `cli.py` has no `if __name__ == \"__main__\":` block.\n\nUse a disposable database path when you want a clean run:\n\n```bash\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc-orders.sqlite python3 -c \"from minisvc.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\"\n```\n\n## Local smoke test command\nThere is no test suite in this fixture. Use a direct smoke script against the real handlers and repository:\n\n```bash\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport sqlite3\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\nfrom minisvc.api.handlers import create_order, get_order\n\ntmpdir = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\ndb = str(Path(tmpdir.name) / 'orders.sqlite')\nrepo = OrderRepository(db)\nrepo.init_schema()\nprint(create_order({'order_id': 'o-1', 'customer': 'Taylor', 'total_cents': '42'}, repo))\nprint(get_order('o-1', repo))\nwith sqlite3.connect(db) as conn:\n    print(conn.execute(\"select order_id, customer, total_cents from orders\").fetchall())\nPY\n```\n\n## First breakpoint or trace point\nSet your first breakpoint at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order`.\n\nWhy there:\n- It is the narrowest point where request data becomes an `Order`.\n- You can inspect payload assumptions, `int()` coercion, repository calls, and the inline audit event in one stop.\n- Most near-term bugs will show up here before they spread into framework glue.\n\nIf you prefer tracing over breakpoints, log the payload and the `repo.save(order)` call boundary in `create_order` while using a temporary SQLite file.\n\n## Runtime flow to internalize\n1. Console entry point calls `minisvc.cli:main`.\n2. `main` loads settings from environment.\n3. `main` instantiates `OrderRepository` and initializes schema.\n4. External HTTP integration calls `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo)`.\n5. POST `/orders` reaches `create_order`; GET `/orders/<order_id>` reaches `get_order`.\n6. Repository methods open SQLite connections per operation.\n7. Audit data is returned in responses only; it is not persisted.\n\n## Two safe first changes\n1. Add targeted request validation in `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order` so missing fields and non-integer totals return controlled errors instead of raw exceptions.\n2. Add a small integration-style test file that exercises `OrderRepository.init_schema`, `create_order`, and `get_order` against a temporary SQLite database.\n\nBoth changes are low-risk, local, and teach the real runtime boundaries without redesigning the service.\n"},"intent":"Writing onboarding plan"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":5094,"output":1959,"cacheRead":23040,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30093,"reasoningTokens":11,"cost":{"input":0.012735000000000002,"output":0.029385,"cacheRead":0.0057599999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.047880000000000006}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788183447566,"responseId":"resp_03f8569485436378016a958397ddc887d2bb597d9e88c6f5e0","duration":36470.82557799999,"ttft":1055.2215979999746},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCal